matched_variant_raw.rewritten_question_text:
Ammonia and nitrous oxide undergo the following reaction:

$$2\mathrm{NH_3(g)} + 3\mathrm{N_2O(g)} \rightarrow 4\mathrm{N_2(g)} + 3\mathrm{H_2O(g)}$$

The enthalpy values of various bonds are known:
the $\mathrm{N-H}$ bond enthalpy is $388\mathrm{kJ/mol}$;
the $\mathrm{N-O}$ bond enthalpy is $210\mathrm{kJ/mol}$;
the $\mathrm{N=O}$ bond enthalpy is $630\mathrm{kJ/mol}$;
the $\mathrm{N=N}$ bond enthalpy is $409\mathrm{kJ/mol}$;
the $\mathrm{N\equiv N}$ bond enthalpy is $941\mathrm{kJ/mol}$;
the $\mathrm{O-H}$ bond enthalpy is $463\mathrm{kJ/mol}$.

(1) According to the absolute entropy value chart, calculate the total entropy change of this reaction ($\mathrm{J/mol\cdot K}$);
(2) Calculate the total enthalpy change of this reaction ($\mathrm{kJ/mol}$).

